  "aiMeta": {
    "narrative": "The rule turns an Emirates checked-baggage quote request into an allowance-and-cost response. It first seeds a working object with every output field, then copies the request's cabin, requested extra-bag count and loyalty tier into it. A reference lookup against the loyalty-tiers table resolves the customer's tier rank (Blue=1 … Platinum=4), defaulting to 0 when no tier is supplied. The base free allowance is then chosen by cabin: First=50kg, Business=40kg, otherwise Economy=30kg. A loyalty bonus of 5kg per tier rank is added, and the two are summed into the total free allowance offered. Finally the extra-bag charge is computed as the number of extra bags multiplied by the flat per-bag fee, and the enriched working object is returned.",
    "nodeExplanations": {
      "n2": "Seeds the working object with all fields used downstream (allowances, fees, currency) so later nodes only need to overwrite values.",
      "n3": "Copies the request's cabin class, extra-bag count and loyalty tier onto the working object.",
      "n4": "Looks up the loyalty tier's numeric rank from the loyalty-tiers reference table; leaves the seeded 0 if the tier is absent.",
      "n5": "Sets the base free checked allowance from the cabin: First 50kg, Business 40kg, Economy 30kg.",
      "n6": "Adds a loyalty bonus of 5kg for each tier rank the member holds.",
      "n7": "Sums base allowance and loyalty bonus into the total free baggage offered to the customer.",
      "n8": "Multiplies the requested number of extra bags by the per-bag fee to produce the total extra-bag cost."
    },
